WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:16.050
X fifteen is the First Isodynamic Point of triangle A B C: construct the three Apollonian circles passing through each vertex and the interior and exterior angle bisector feet on the opposite side, and all three circles intersect inside the circumcircle at X fifteen.

2
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:28.146
Its trilinear coordinates are sine of A plus pi over three, to sine of B plus pi over three, to sine of C plus pi over three— the exact reciprocals of the Fermat point X thirteen.

3
00:00:28.146 --> 00:00:32.452
Remarkably, the pedal triangle of X fifteen is always equilateral!

4
00:00:32.452 --> 00:00:39.040
On the central lines layer, X fifteen lies on the Brocard axis through X three, X six, and X sixteen.

5
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:48.180
X fifteen is the isogonal conjugate of the Fermat point X thirteen, and the circumcircle inverse of the Second Isodynamic Point X sixteen.
